    {
      "file": "scenes/scene-2.js",
      "narration": "The audience knows where to look. What they see stays in step with what they hear. And in a video, every new idea means a fresh picture on screen.",
      "minDuration": 10,
      "slide": {
        "title": "Why the rule works",
        "text": "The audience knows where to look. What they see matches what they hear. It works better as video. Easier to update",
        "notes": "The audience knows where to look. What they see stays in step with what they hear. And in a video, every new idea means a fresh picture on screen.",
        "image": "assets/slide-3.png"
      },
      "storyboard": "three glowing icon-orbs build in a row, one per phrase: an eye / focus ring on 'where to look', an ear plus eye linked by a pulsing line on 'in step with what they hear', then a film strip whose frames flip through different pictures on 'fresh picture'. Each orb lights up on its phrase while the others dim.",
